# Completion Reporting

When a milestone or task requires a completion report, include **all** of the following sections.

## Required sections

### Summary
What was delivered and why, in a few sentences.

### Files Created
Bullet list of new paths.

### Files Modified
Bullet list of changed paths (or “None”).

### Tests Executed
Commands run and outcome, or “None (documentation-only)”.

### Migration Impact
Alembic/schema effects. Use **None** when no migrations were added or changed.

### Architecture Compliance
Confirm layering and especially **curriculum V1/V2** invariants. State whether traversal/import compatibility was preserved or N/A.

### Technical Debt
Honest leftover risk or follow-ups introduced by this work (or “None”).

### Known Limitations
Boundaries of what this milestone did not solve.

## Required sections for EP / P programmes

Every future **EP** or **P** programme completion report must **also** include:

### Student Impact Assessment
Completed assessment using `knowledge/product/p001_1_ksi_baseline/STUDENT_IMPACT_ASSESSMENT_TEMPLATE.md` (or equivalent sections with a link to that template). Cover student problem, student benefit, learning benefit, success metrics, risks, and assumptions. Architectural blast-radius tables may supplement but do not replace student-value sections.

### Estimated KSI contribution
Category deltas for K1–K8 and net ΔKSI per `knowledge/product/p001_1_ksi_baseline/PRODUCT_SUCCESS_FRAMEWORK.md`. Infra/docs-only work may record ΔKSI = 0 with rationale.

### Evidence collected
Paths to tests, reviews, metrics, interviews, dogfood, or other evidence supporting claims.

### Lessons learned for student value
What the programme taught about educational usefulness — including what failed to move perceived student value.

### Explainability Review (when in scope)
If the programme affects student-facing intelligence (recommendations, predictions, planning, readiness, Coach/Insights, or related Runtime A guidance), complete `knowledge/product/p001_2_explainability_standard/EXPLAINABILITY_REVIEW_CHECKLIST.md` per `knowledge/GOVERNANCE.md` §4.2. Docs/infra-only work may record N/A with rationale. K8 claims require checklist Pass (or waiver).

### Recommendation Quality Review (when in scope)
If the programme affects student-facing recommendations (ranking, selection, Coach/Insights/Mission tips, revision/recovery/workload recommendations, or Runtime A primary-recommendation consolidation), complete `knowledge/product/p001_3_recommendation_quality_standard/RECOMMENDATION_REVIEW_CHECKLIST.md` per `knowledge/GOVERNANCE.md` §4.3. Docs/infra-only work may record N/A with rationale. K2 claims require checklist Pass (or waiver).

### Version 1 readiness residual (when claiming V1 progress)
If the programme claims progress toward **Version 1 production-ready**, cite residual open gates from `knowledge/product/p002_1_version_1_release_framework/VERSION_1_RELEASE_FRAMEWORK.md` (G1–G12). Docs/governance programmes that only define release law may record N/A. Estimated ΔKSI alone does not satisfy Gate G1 (validated KSI required for declaration).

Version 1 product-success claims require **KSI ≥ 80** under the Product Success Framework. Version 1 **production-ready** declaration additionally requires the P-002.1 Release Framework gates and evidence package. KSI does not replace Vision 2030’s north star.

## Rules

- Be specific to Kwalitec — no placeholder lorem.
- Call out if application code was intentionally untouched.
- Include the commit hash when the milestone requires a commit.
- After the mandated commit/stop instruction, do not start the next milestone.
